<title>BANGLADESH: Strike shuts Bangladesh's Mongla port.</title>
<headline>Strike shuts Bangladesh's Mongla port.</headline>
<dateline>KHULNA, Bangladesh 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearly 6,500 workers at Bangladesh's southern Mongla port stopped work on Tuesday over a wage dispute, stranding 22 foreign ships, port officials said.</p>
<p>They said the workers started an indefinite strike after port authorities refused to meet their demands for higher wages and bonus payments ahead of the Moslem festival of Eid al-Fitr next month.</p>
<p>&quot;Their demand is too much and it will be difficult for the government to satisfy them,&quot; one official said.</p>
<p>Of the 22 ships, six were carrying fertiliser and four cement.</p>
<p>Officials said authorities were negotiating with unionists to try to end the stoppage.</p>
</text>
